<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             x:Class="CRT.RebuildManifestsView">

    <!--
    REBUILD CHECKSUM MANIFESTS (owner request, 2026-10-01: "I need a way ... to press a button, and
    then it will generate a new online manifest, both for production and BETA ... when testing a
    lot, I need to do some manual editing of files from time to time, and then I need it to update
    the checksum again"). ADMINISTRATOR ONLY, like every padlocked entry on the Account screen (the Admin screen until 2026-10-04).

    ONE BUTTON FOR BOTH TREES (owner decision, same day). A hand edit is as likely in one as the
    other, and rebuilding a tree that did not change costs only the scan - what it writes is
    identical. The server decides which trees exist; this panel shows what it answered.

    NO CONFIRMATION, deliberately: a rebuild reads the tree and replaces one file atomically. It
    destroys nothing and can simply be pressed again. What it DOES need is to say what happened, so
    every tree's own result is listed under the headline.

    All the words are the SERVER's (ManifestRebuildFlow), shown unchanged - a server that gains a
    third tree says so with no CRT release.
    -->
    <DockPanel>

        <TextBlock DockPanel.Dock="Top"
                   Text="Rebuild checksum manifests"
                   FontWeight="SemiBold"
                   FontSize="14"
                   Margin="0,0,0,8" />

        <TextBlock DockPanel.Dock="Top"
                   TextWrapping="Wrap"
                   Opacity="0.8"
                   Margin="0,0,0,12"
                   Text="Every board CRT downloads is checked against dataChecksums.json. The server rebuilds it by itself whenever it publishes, promotes or rolls back - so this is only needed after data files have been changed on the server by hand, which the service never sees. Both the BETA and the stable data are rebuilt." />

        <Button DockPanel.Dock="Top"
                x:Name="RebuildButton"
                HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                Content="Rebuild both manifests"
                Margin="0,0,0,12"
                Click="OnRebuildClick" />

        <TextBlock DockPanel.Dock="Top"
                   x:Name="HeadlineText"
                   TextWrapping="Wrap"
                   FontWeight="SemiBold"
                   IsVisible="False"
                   Margin="0,0,0,8" />

        <!-- One line per tree, in the server's words. Not a ScrollViewer: there are two of them. -->
        <StackPanel DockPanel.Dock="Top"
                    x:Name="ResultsPanel"
                    Spacing="4" />

        <TextBlock x:Name="MessageText"
                   DockPanel.Dock="Top"
                   TextWrapping="Wrap"
                   IsVisible="False"
                   Margin="0,8,0,0" />

        <!-- Nothing fills the rest; the panel is a header, a button and its answer. -->
        <Panel />
    </DockPanel>
</UserControl>
